loadavg 0.96 0.47 0.52 8/314 209873
governor {"0": "absent", "1": "absent", "2": "absent", "3": "absent", "4": "absent", "5": "absent", "6": "absent", "7": "absent"}
cpu_mhz 2700.0
warm reads the file once before the clock; cold drops the page cache after warmup
every timed read copies positions and the cell into numpy and checks the sum
note chemfiles has no native CON format; the chemfiles-con row copies positions and the cell out of a chemfiles Frame filled from readcon.
note chemfiles compression library /tmp/chemfiles-install/lib/libchemfiles.so opens {"bz2": true, "gz": true, "trr": true, "xz": true}
note MDAnalysis 2.11.0 on DCD, XTC, NetCDF, TRR, XYZ and PDB. Cells are orthogonal, so the 2.11 triclinic wrap does not apply.
note mdcompress 2.0.5 (refresh-bio). 1.0.0 is not on PyPI and this row is not relabeled as 1.0.0. Archive preset, one thread. The clock compresses a DCD that is already on disk, and the read queries one frame at a time. A one-frame trajectory cannot be read ('Cannot read first frame' on DCD, XTC and TRR), so those rows are unsupported. The binding views the float64 box as float32; the cell is read from those bytes as float64.
